 ## Background
-3D Trilinear Interpolation is a standard technique in computer graphics and scientific visualization for sampling dense grid data. It is widely used in volume rendering, particularly in raycasting, to sample voxel values at sub-voxel precision [S1]. The method is fundamental to many volume rendering pipelines, including those using spherical harmonics for view-dependent effects [S2].
